abstract: 'Computational forensic linguistics analysis of vaccine hesitancy discourse by Children''s Health Defense state chapters on Twitter/X. Applies PMI lexical association analysis (Church & Hanks, 1990), epistemic stance classification (Heritage, 2012), and multimodal fear appeals framework (Gill & Lennon, 2022) to examine how anti-vaccine organizations construct persuasive health misinformation through coordinated linguistic and visual strategies.'
